This supports not using history/memory as evidence, but \"tool events or reports\" — actually the report does use the report? Hmm. The report itself is the output. Let me check.\n\nActually the trajectory report: \"逐字引用如何交付：... 参考对象只用资料工具返回的 ResourceRef，不使用历史或记忆充当资料证据。\" This says only ResourceRef from source tool, not history or memory. It doesn't explicitly say \"tool events or reports.\"\n\nActually wait, the candidate memory says \"Never treat tool events or reports as evidence\". The trajectory shows tool events include read_source which IS the source reading. Hmm, actually read_source is the tool that reads the licensed source. The report uses read_source results.\n\nLet me think more carefully about grounded. The core workflow in the skill is: confirm allowed sources correspond to licensed directory, use read_source to read full text, classify fields (fact vs unknown), record verbatim strings, attach ResourceRef + location + verbatim excerpt, preserve unknown, re-verify excerpts.\n\nThe trajectory report describes exactly this. So grounded is largely true.\n\nNow the memory's statement \"Never treat tool events or reports as evidence—only licensed primary sources count.\" Is this supported by trajectory? The trajectory says \"参考对象只用资料工具返回的 ResourceRef，不使用历史或记忆充当资料证据。\" This is about not using history/memory, and using ResourceRef. It doesn't mention \"tool events or reports.\"\n\nHmm, but actually the trajectory report distinguishes that the read_source returns the licensed primary source content. The \"tool events\" is the mechanism. The candidate memory phrase \"tool events or reports\" might be slightly over-generalizing. But let me think about whether this matters.\n\nActually, let me focus on the key checks.\n\nPrivacy_safe: The candidate doesn't contain any specific resource IDs, filenames, values, or identities. Let me check.\n\nMemory: \"When verifying fields for acceptance, first check if the source explicitly asserts a value (fact) or explicitly dec